  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Saints Simon and Jude, Apostles” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, Jesus said to His disciples: “These things I command you, that you love one another. If the world hates you, know that it held Me in hatred before you. If you had been of the world, the world would love what was its own; but since you are not of the world, but rather I chose you out of the world, for that reason the world hates you. Remember the word that I spoke to you: ‘The servant is not greater than his master.’ If they have persecuted Me, they will persecute you also; if they have kept My word, they will keep yours also. But all these things they will do to you on account of My name, because they do not know Him who sent Me. Had I not come and spoken to them, they would not have sin; but now they have no excuse concerning their sin. He who hates Me hates My Father also. Had I not done among them works which no one else did, they would not have sin; but now they have both seen and hated both Me and My Father. But this is so that the word may be fulfilled which is written in their law: ‘They held Me in hatred without cause.’”", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w024"], "reason": "idiom" }, { "words": ["w065", "w066"], "anchor": "w065", "gloss": "persecuted" }, { "words": ["w095", "w096"], "anchor": "w095", "gloss": "spoken" }, { "words": ["w152"], "reason": "idiom" }] }
  },
